status: accept
exit: 42
covers: op_symbol is_clause place_uses_clause law_quantifiers law_quantifier law_decl
note: |
  An algebra is a place written `is algebra` at a root: its operations and its laws,
  stated with the symbols of logic over its own name. A place that `uses
  algebra` is a model: it gives each operation as its own fun, and every law
  is certified on it (here exhaustively, on the two arms of Coin). A place
  `this <` an algebra is an algebra without writing it: Plus32, an instance
  on i32 below Monoid, whose laws are axioms there (`is given`).
